From a72d63a188c5dddc8368437f74dd4094d8ca9887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Duncan <JonathanDuncan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:31:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add TLS_PSK_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 and
 TLS_ECDHE_PSK_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256

DTLS 1.2, client and server. ECDHE_PSK (RFC 5489): the ServerKeyExchange carries
the identity hint then unsigned ECDH parameters, the ClientKeyExchange the
identity then the client's point, and the pre-master secret is
uint16(len Z) || Z || uint16(len psk) || psk. Record protection reuses the
existing AES-128-GCM and ChaCha20-Poly1305 ciphers. The PSK tests run over all
three PSK suites.
